# LitTrans project: keep the record in, keep the source out.
#
# Tracked: what a later batch run or audit needs to reproduce or check the work — the
# extraction (derived/units.jsonl, the asset crops and their evidence), the page receipts
# and review packets they name, the translation, QA reports, review ledgers and the
# packets each agent was actually shown. Ignored: the copyrighted source PDF and anything
# regenerable. Never add a public remote: the record embeds excerpts of the source.
#
# Verify after editing: `littrans project tracked PROJECT` asks git whether exactly the
# record is tracked and reports every gap.

# The source PDF, never redistributed.
source/
*.pdf

# Runtime state. state.json is the write lock; .littrans/work/ holds the exact packet
# payload each translator or reviewer was given and is named by packet id in the audit
# ledger, so it is part of the record.
{% for line in ignore_lines %}
{{ line }}
{% endfor %}
.littrans-write-lock/

# Regenerable from the record.
output/
derived/assets/fidelity/*/original.pdf

# Layout detector results (derived/fidelity-layout/<fingerprint>.json) are evidence the
# page ledgers name: a rerun on any host cuts each page on its recorded result, and no
# other detector runtime reproduces the fingerprint. The request and log of a detection
# run carry this host's paths and interpreter and stay out.
derived/fidelity-layout/*.request.json
derived/fidelity-layout/*.log

# Source review packets duplicate tracked tables, except the ones page receipts name:
# those are live dependencies of the review. `project tracked` lists them; re-include
# each live packet below by name, e.g.
#   !packets/source-<id>/packet.json
#   !packets/source-<id>/coverage.html
packets/*/packet.json
packets/*/coverage.html

# Editor and Python noise.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
